2571
01:49:42,910 --> 01:49:47,247
<i>And you sprayed me when I was
giving notes to Chiwetel, didn't you?</i>

2572
01:49:47,331 --> 01:49:48,791
<i>I which?
You sprayed me.</i>

2573
01:49:48,874 --> 01:49:51,543
<i>For part of the scene that got cut,
I was giving notes to Chiwetet,</i>

2574
01:49:51,627 --> 01:49:55,255
<i>and I was standing and you just took
the little thing, gave me a little spray.</i>

2575
01:49:55,339 --> 01:49:57,966
<i>Good times. Yeah.</i>

2576
01:49:58,467 --> 01:50:00,969
<i>Just so I'd remember
who's captain and who's not.</i>

2577
01:50:01,053 --> 01:50:02,763
<i>(FILLLON GIGGLING)</i>

2578
01:50:03,013 --> 01:50:06,100
<i>BALDWIN: 80 about how much time
has passed here? A month, six months?</i>

2579
01:50:06,183 --> 01:50:08,477
<i>WHEDON: Well, you've built
the ship up completely</i>

2580
01:50:08,560 --> 01:50:10,399
<i>and you're all totally
healed from your wounds,</i>

2581
01:50:10,479 --> 01:50:12,481
<i>so I say it's probably,
like, three days.</i>

2582
01:50:12,564 --> 01:50:14,566
<i>(ALL LAUGHING)</i>

2583
01:50:14,775 --> 01:50:18,612
<i>Um, I always imagined
it as about a month.</i>

2584
01:50:18,695 --> 01:50:21,031
There is nothing left to see.

2585
01:50:25,244 --> 01:50:27,246
<i>I sort of pull a
little fast into this.</i>

2586
01:50:27,329 --> 01:50:28,959
<i>FILLLON: This was the
scene that I had no idea</i>

2587
01:50:29,039 --> 01:50:30,377
<i>what it was about until
you told me that day.</i>

2588
01:50:30,457 --> 01:50:32,584
<i>WHEDON: Yeah, yeah,
which always made me laugh,</i>

2589
01:50:32,668 --> 01:50:33,964
<i>'cause you were so
precise about meaning,</i>

2590
01:50:34,044 --> 01:50:35,921
<i>and then you were, like,
"This about what now?"</i>

2591
01:50:36,004 --> 01:50:38,549
<i>(LAUGHING) Just
something I missed.</i>

2592
01:50:41,051 --> 01:50:42,594
<i>It's tough, too.</i>

2593
01:50:43,053 --> 01:50:46,014
<i>'Cause, again, the dialogue,
"She'll fly true."</i>

2594
01:50:46,181 --> 01:50:49,268
<i>That's a hard thing to
say and not sound hokey.</i>

2595
01:50:49,393 --> 01:50:51,645
<i>And Gina... Unless
you're talking about her.</i>

2596
01:50:51,728 --> 01:50:53,897
<i>Yeah. She's got
a lot of dignity.</i>

2597
01:50:53,981 --> 01:50:58,735
<i>She's got all the dignity. In fact,
none of you guys had any 'cause she took it.</i>

2598
01:51:00,112 --> 01:51:02,576
<i>BALDWIN: I don't want dignity. All right,
Ron, you had a little.</i>

2599
01:51:02,656 --> 01:51:04,995
<i>FILLLON: I'm sorry, man. You had
great arms in that show and everything</i>

2600
01:51:05,075 --> 01:51:08,495
<i>but you ran a close second
to Gina Torres' pipes.</i>

2601
01:51:08,579 --> 01:51:10,664
Ready to get off this heap,
back to civilized life?

2602
01:51:10,747 --> 01:51:11,790
I, uh...

2603
01:51:11,874 --> 01:51:14,751
<i>BALDWIN: Actually, I ended up with
food on my face. That's all I wanted.</i>

2604
01:51:14,835 --> 01:51:16,295
<i>WHEDON: Yeah,
the food was great!</i>

2605
01:51:16,378 --> 01:51:18,755
<i>The food was full
of Chinese noodles.</i>

2606
01:51:20,090 --> 01:51:21,300
Good answer.

2607
01:51:21,675 --> 01:51:24,511
<i>WHEDON: I don't not love
that line, really.</i>

2608
01:51:30,934 --> 01:51:33,103
<i>This is the part
we were talking about.</i>

2609
01:51:33,187 --> 01:51:35,692
<i>FILLLON: Yeah, there was an adjustment
on one of the fallen dinosaurs there.</i>

2610
01:51:35,772 --> 01:51:38,192
<i>Summer, your thoughts
on this scene?</i>

2611
01:51:38,275 --> 01:51:39,693
<i>Last chance.</i>

2612
01:51:39,943 --> 01:51:41,528
<i>I liked the raining part.</i>

2613
01:51:41,612 --> 01:51:44,198
<i>Where it was raining.
The rain was really nice.</i>

2614
01:51:44,281 --> 01:51:47,367
<i>It really felt like it.
It was kind of cold.</i>

2615
01:51:47,451 --> 01:51:51,538
<i>FILLLON: I know for a fact that Summer
had designs on being the captain.</i>

2616
01:51:51,622 --> 01:51:53,457
<i>I still do.</i>

2617
01:51:55,167 --> 01:51:57,628
<i>WHEDON: "First,
I learn to fly it."</i>

2618
01:52:01,465 --> 01:52:03,467
<i>Just evil.</i>

2619
01:52:03,842 --> 01:52:06,011
<i>All she ever was.</i>

2620
01:52:08,472 --> 01:52:10,224
<i>But I'm saving that
for the sequel.</i>

2621
01:52:10,307 --> 01:52:12,601
You know what the
first rule of flying is?

2622
01:52:12,684 --> 01:52:17,064
Well, I suppose you do,
since you already know what I'm about to say.

2623
01:52:18,273 --> 01:52:19,987
<i>WHEDON: Well, looks like
we're winding down.</i>

2624
01:52:20,067 --> 01:52:22,694
<i>FILLLON: We are. We 're
Winding down. All in all...</i>

2625
01:52:22,778 --> 01:52:24,613
<i>GLASS: I'd have been
a good captain.</i>

2626
01:52:24,696 --> 01:52:27,866
<i>Oh, Ron.
I would.</i>

2627
01:52:27,950 --> 01:52:29,288
You can learn all the
math in the 'verse,

2628
01:52:29,368 --> 01:52:31,912
but you take a boat in
the air that you don't love...

2629
01:52:31,995 --> 01:52:34,498
<i>(ALL LAUGHING)</i>

2630
01:52:35,290 --> 01:52:38,752
<i>FILLLON: All in all, I'd have to say,
the TV series and the film,</i>

2631
01:52:38,835 --> 01:52:40,921
<i>very, very good experience.</i>

2632
01:52:41,004 --> 01:52:44,633
<i>I learned a great deal,
I had an amazing time,</i>

2633
01:52:44,716 --> 01:52:48,971
<i>I've acquired many awesome
friends for which my life is richer.</i>

2634
01:52:49,054 --> 01:52:51,348
<i>WHEDON:
And I met you guys, too.</i>

2635
01:52:53,684 --> 01:52:55,602
<i>Bittersweet.
It's bittersweet.</i>

2636
01:52:55,686 --> 01:52:57,437
<i>Like that chocolate that's dark.</i>

2637
01:52:57,521 --> 01:53:00,899
<i>You know what? I always say that,
but I'm all over the bitter.</i>

2638
01:53:01,024 --> 01:53:02,609
<i>Yeah. All the
bitter's gone for me.</i>

2639
01:53:02,693 --> 01:53:05,612
<i>I don't live by it</i>

2640
01:53:05,696 --> 01:53:06,947
<i>but I can access it.</i>

2641
01:53:07,030 --> 01:53:08,660
<i>(FILLLON LAUGHING)</i>

2642
01:53:08,740 --> 01:53:13,203
<i>BALDWIN: I always try to keep
this in the mind of redemption.</i>

2643
01:53:14,204 --> 01:53:19,126
<i>That we made something good
and we finished with something good.</i>

2644
01:53:19,876 --> 01:53:22,379
<i>And you can't control
the audience.</i>

2645
01:53:22,462 --> 01:53:23,630
<i>FILLLON: Thank you.</i>

2646
01:53:23,714 --> 01:53:25,090
<i>(ALL LAUGHING)</i>

2647
01:53:25,173 --> 01:53:26,800
<i>WHEDON: That's it.</i>

2648
01:53:26,883 --> 01:53:28,802
<i>BALDWIN: Well,
that'll be all, guys.</i>

2649
01:53:28,885 --> 01:53:31,888
<i>We went through it and now
we're through it and it's through.</i>

